{
  "version": 1,
  "id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000108",
  "title": "Double Pendulum",
  "created_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "shared_cargo_toml": "[profile.release]\nopt-level = 1\nlto = false\ncodegen-units = 16",
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "cell_intro",
      "order": 0,
      "label": "Introduction",
      "cell_type": "Markdown",
      "source": "> *AI authored to showcase ironpad capabilities.*\n\n# Double Pendulum — Chaos in Motion 🎯\n\nThe **double pendulum** is one of the simplest physical systems that exhibits **chaotic behavior**. Two rigid rods connected end-to-end, swinging under gravity — yet the motion is wildly unpredictable.\n\n## Lagrangian Mechanics\n\nInstead of tracking forces, we use the **Lagrangian** $L = T - V$ (kinetic minus potential energy) and derive equations of motion from the **Euler–Lagrange equation**:\n\n$$\\frac{d}{dt}\\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial \\dot{\\theta}} - \\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial \\theta} = 0$$\n\nFor a double pendulum with masses $m_1, m_2$ and rod lengths $\\ell_1, \\ell_2$, the resulting equations are coupled, nonlinear, and **have no closed-form solution** — making numerical simulation essential.\n\n## This Notebook\n\nUse the **sliders** below to tune the physical parameters, then watch the **simulation** respond in real time. The second bob leaves a fading trail that reveals the chaotic trajectory. The **energy dashboard** monitors KE, PE, and total mechanical energy to verify numerical accuracy.\n\n**Integration**: 4th-order Runge–Kutta with 10 sub-steps per frame for stability.",
      "cargo_toml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_controls",
      "order": 1,
      "label": "Parameter Controls",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "(\n    ui::slider(\"l1\", 50.0, 200.0)\n        .step(1.0)\n        .label(\"Length L₁\")\n        .default_value(120.0),\n    ui::slider(\"l2\", 50.0, 200.0)\n        .step(1.0)\n        .label(\"Length L₂\")\n        .default_value(120.0),\n    ui::slider(\"m1\", 1.0, 10.0)\n        .step(0.1)\n        .label(\"Mass m₁\")\n        .default_value(2.0),\n    ui::slider(\"m2\", 1.0, 10.0)\n        .step(0.1)\n        .label(\"Mass m₂\")\n        .default_value(2.0),\n    ui::slider(\"theta1\", 0.0, 360.0)\n        .step(1.0)\n        .label(\"Initial θ₁ (°)\")\n        .default_value(120.0),\n    ui::slider(\"theta2\", 0.0, 360.0)\n        .step(1.0)\n        .label(\"Initial θ₂ (°)\")\n        .default_value(150.0),\n)",
      "cargo_toml": null,
      "collapsed": true
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_sim",
      "order": 2,
      "label": "Live Simulation",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "// Double Pendulum — live Simulation trait implementation.\n//\n// RK4 integration of the Lagrangian equations of motion with a fading\n// trail. Parameters are read from the shared bus each tick; energy data\n// is published for the dashboard cell.\n\nconst WIDTH: u32 = 800;\nconst HEIGHT: u32 = 800;\nconst G: f64 = 9.81;\nconst PIVOT_X: f64 = 400.0;\nconst PIVOT_Y: f64 = 178.0;\nconst MAX_TRAIL: usize = 500;\nconst SUB_STEPS: usize = 10;\nconst DT: f64 = 1.0 / 60.0;\n// Pixel length corresponding to 1.0 in physics units (meters).\nconst REF_PX: f64 = 120.0;\n\nstruct DoublePendulum {\n    theta1: f64,\n    omega1: f64,\n    theta2: f64,\n    omega2: f64,\n    trail: Vec<(f64, f64)>,\n    // Previous angle slider values — used to detect reset.\n    prev_t1_deg: f64,\n    prev_t2_deg: f64,\n}\n\n// ── Physics ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n/// Derivatives [dθ₁/dt, dθ₂/dt, dω₁/dt, dω₂/dt] from the Lagrangian EOM.\nfn derivs(t1: f64, t2: f64, w1: f64, w2: f64, m1: f64, m2: f64, l1: f64, l2: f64) -> [f64; 4] {\n    let delta = t1 - t2;\n    let sin_d = delta.sin();\n    let cos_d = delta.cos();\n    let denom = 2.0 * m1 + m2 - m2 * (2.0 * delta).cos();\n\n    let alpha1 = (-G * (2.0 * m1 + m2) * t1.sin()\n        - m2 * G * (t1 - 2.0 * t2).sin()\n        - 2.0 * sin_d * m2 * (w2 * w2 * l2 + w1 * w1 * l1 * cos_d))\n        / (l1 * denom);\n\n    let alpha2 = (2.0 * sin_d\n        * (w1 * w1 * l1 * (m1 + m2)\n            + G * (m1 + m2) * t1.cos()\n            + w2 * w2 * l2 * m2 * cos_d))\n        / (l2 * denom);\n\n    [w1, w2, alpha1, alpha2]\n}\n\n/// Advance state by one RK4 step of size `dt`.\nfn rk4_step(\n    t1: &mut f64, t2: &mut f64, w1: &mut f64, w2: &mut f64,\n    m1: f64, m2: f64, l1: f64, l2: f64, dt: f64,\n) {\n    let k1 = derivs(*t1, *t2, *w1, *w2, m1, m2, l1, l2);\n    let k2 = derivs(\n        *t1 + 0.5 * dt * k1[0], *t2 + 0.5 * dt * k1[1],\n        *w1 + 0.5 * dt * k1[2], *w2 + 0.5 * dt * k1[3],\n        m1, m2, l1, l2,\n    );\n    let k3 = derivs(\n        *t1 + 0.5 * dt * k2[0], *t2 + 0.5 * dt * k2[1],\n        *w1 + 0.5 * dt * k2[2], *w2 + 0.5 * dt * k2[3],\n        m1, m2, l1, l2,\n    );\n    let k4 = derivs(\n        *t1 + dt * k3[0], *t2 + dt * k3[1],\n        *w1 + dt * k3[2], *w2 + dt * k3[3],\n        m1, m2, l1, l2,\n    );\n\n    *t1 += (dt / 6.0) * (k1[0] + 2.0 * k2[0] + 2.0 * k3[0] + k4[0]);\n    *t2 += (dt / 6.0) * (k1[1] + 2.0 * k2[1] + 2.0 * k3[1] + k4[1]);\n    *w1 += (dt / 6.0) * (k1[2] + 2.0 * k2[2] + 2.0 * k3[2] + k4[2]);\n    *w2 += (dt / 6.0) * (k1[3] + 2.0 * k2[3] + 2.0 * k3[3] + k4[3]);\n}\n\n// ── Drawing helpers ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nfn draw_line(canvas: &mut Canvas, x0: i32, y0: i32, x1: i32, y1: i32, color: (u8, u8, u8)) {\n    let dx = (x1 - x0).abs();\n    let dy = -(y1 - y0).abs();\n    let sx: i32 = if x0 < x1 { 1 } else { -1 };\n    let sy: i32 = if y0 < y1 { 1 } else { -1 };\n    let mut err = dx + dy;\n    let (mut x, mut y) = (x0, y0);\n\n    loop {\n        if x >= 0 && y >= 0 {\n            canvas.set_pixel(x as u32, y as u32, color);\n        }\n        if x == x1 && y == y1 { break; }\n        let e2 = 2 * err;\n        if e2 >= dy { err += dy; x += sx; }\n        if e2 <= dx { err += dx; y += sy; }\n    }\n}\n\nfn draw_thick_line(\n    canvas: &mut Canvas,\n    x0: i32, y0: i32, x1: i32, y1: i32,\n    thickness: i32, color: (u8, u8, u8),\n) {\n    for oy in -thickness..=thickness {\n        for ox in -thickness..=thickness {\n            if ox * ox + oy * oy <= thickness * thickness {\n                draw_line(canvas, x0 + ox, y0 + oy, x1 + ox, y1 + oy, color);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nfn draw_circle(canvas: &mut Canvas, cx: i32, cy: i32, r: i32, color: (u8, u8, u8)) {\n    for dy in -r..=r {\n        for dx in -r..=r {\n            if dx * dx + dy * dy <= r * r {\n                let px = cx + dx;\n                let py = cy + dy;\n                if px >= 0 && py >= 0 {\n                    canvas.set_pixel(px as u32, py as u32, color);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// ── Simulation trait ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nimpl Simulation for DoublePendulum {\n    fn init() -> Self {\n        let t1_deg = 120.0_f64;\n        let t2_deg = 150.0_f64;\n        Self {\n            theta1: t1_deg.to_radians(),\n            omega1: 0.0,\n            theta2: t2_deg.to_radians(),\n            omega2: 0.0,\n            trail: Vec::with_capacity(MAX_TRAIL),\n            prev_t1_deg: t1_deg,\n            prev_t2_deg: t2_deg,\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn tick(&mut self) -> Canvas {\n        // Read parameters from the bus (populated by the slider cell).\n        let l1_px = sim::read::<f64>(\"l1\").unwrap_or(120.0);\n        let l2_px = sim::read::<f64>(\"l2\").unwrap_or(120.0);\n        let m1    = sim::read::<f64>(\"m1\").unwrap_or(2.0);\n        let m2    = sim::read::<f64>(\"m2\").unwrap_or(2.0);\n        let t1_deg = sim::read::<f64>(\"theta1\").unwrap_or(120.0);\n        let t2_deg = sim::read::<f64>(\"theta2\").unwrap_or(150.0);\n\n        // Physics lengths: REF_PX pixels == 1.0 meter.\n        let l1 = l1_px / REF_PX;\n        let l2 = l2_px / REF_PX;\n\n        // Reset dynamics when the initial-angle sliders are moved.\n        if (t1_deg - self.prev_t1_deg).abs() > 0.5\n            || (t2_deg - self.prev_t2_deg).abs() > 0.5\n        {\n            self.theta1 = t1_deg.to_radians();\n            self.theta2 = t2_deg.to_radians();\n            self.omega1 = 0.0;\n            self.omega2 = 0.0;\n            self.trail.clear();\n            self.prev_t1_deg = t1_deg;\n            self.prev_t2_deg = t2_deg;\n        }\n\n        // Sub-stepped RK4 integration for numerical stability.\n        let sub_dt = DT / SUB_STEPS as f64;\n        for _ in 0..SUB_STEPS {\n            rk4_step(\n                &mut self.theta1, &mut self.theta2,\n                &mut self.omega1, &mut self.omega2,\n                m1, m2, l1, l2, sub_dt,\n            );\n        }\n\n        // Compute and publish energies for the dashboard.\n        let ke = 0.5 * (m1 + m2) * l1 * l1 * self.omega1 * self.omega1\n            + 0.5 * m2 * l2 * l2 * self.omega2 * self.omega2\n            + m2 * l1 * l2 * self.omega1 * self.omega2 * (self.theta1 - self.theta2).cos();\n        let pe = -(m1 + m2) * G * l1 * self.theta1.cos()\n            - m2 * G * l2 * self.theta2.cos();\n        sim::emit(\"ke\", &ke);\n        sim::emit(\"pe\", &pe);\n        sim::emit(\"omega1\", &self.omega1);\n        sim::emit(\"omega2\", &self.omega2);\n\n        // Bob positions in pixel space.\n        let x1 = PIVOT_X + l1_px * self.theta1.sin();\n        let y1 = PIVOT_Y + l1_px * self.theta1.cos();\n        let x2 = x1 + l2_px * self.theta2.sin();\n        let y2 = y1 + l2_px * self.theta2.cos();\n\n        // Append second bob to the trail.\n        self.trail.push((x2, y2));\n        if self.trail.len() > MAX_TRAIL {\n            self.trail.remove(0);\n        }\n\n        // ── Render ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n        let mut canvas = Canvas::new(WIDTH, HEIGHT);\n        canvas.fill((10, 10, 20));\n\n        // Fading trail: old = dark purple, new = bright magenta.\n        let n = self.trail.len();\n        for (i, &(tx, ty)) in self.trail.iter().enumerate() {\n            let t = i as f64 / n as f64;\n            let r = (40.0 + 215.0 * t) as u8;\n            let g = (10.0 + 70.0 * t) as u8;\n            let b = (60.0 + 140.0 * t) as u8;\n            let px = tx as i32;\n            let py = ty as i32;\n            if px >= 0 && py >= 0 {\n                let ux = px as u32;\n                let uy = py as u32;\n                canvas.set_pixel(ux, uy, (r, g, b));\n                canvas.set_pixel(ux + 1, uy, (r, g, b));\n                canvas.set_pixel(ux, uy + 1, (r, g, b));\n                canvas.set_pixel(ux + 1, uy + 1, (r, g, b));\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Pendulum arms.\n        let arm_color = (200, 200, 210);\n        draw_thick_line(\n            &mut canvas,\n            PIVOT_X as i32, PIVOT_Y as i32, x1 as i32, y1 as i32,\n            1, arm_color,\n        );\n        draw_thick_line(\n            &mut canvas,\n            x1 as i32, y1 as i32, x2 as i32, y2 as i32,\n            1, arm_color,\n        );\n\n        // Pivot.\n        draw_circle(&mut canvas, PIVOT_X as i32, PIVOT_Y as i32, 3, (150, 150, 160));\n\n        // Bobs.\n        draw_circle(&mut canvas, x1 as i32, y1 as i32, 6, (0, 220, 255));\n        draw_circle(&mut canvas, x2 as i32, y2 as i32, 6, (255, 80, 200));\n\n        canvas\n    }\n\n    fn fps() -> u32 {\n        60\n    }\n}",
      "cargo_toml": null,
      "collapsed": true
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_dashboard",
      "order": 3,
      "label": "Energy Dashboard",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "// Energy dashboard — reads KE, PE, and angular velocities published by the\n// simulation cell and renders a live HTML overview at 10 FPS.\n\nstruct Dashboard {\n    tick: u32,\n    initial_total: f64,\n}\n\nimpl LiveView for Dashboard {\n    fn init() -> Self {\n        Self { tick: 0, initial_total: f64::NAN }\n    }\n\n    fn tick(&mut self) -> LiveContent {\n        self.tick += 1;\n        let ke = sim::read::<f64>(\"ke\").unwrap_or(0.0);\n        let pe = sim::read::<f64>(\"pe\").unwrap_or(0.0);\n        let total = ke + pe;\n        let omega1 = sim::read::<f64>(\"omega1\").unwrap_or(0.0);\n        let omega2 = sim::read::<f64>(\"omega2\").unwrap_or(0.0);\n\n        // Capture baseline energy on the first non-zero read.\n        if self.initial_total.is_nan() && total.abs() > 1e-6 {\n            self.initial_total = total;\n        }\n\n        // Bar widths (max 200 px, scale = 80 J full-scale).\n        let scale = 80.0_f64;\n        let ke_bar = ((ke.abs() / scale).min(1.0) * 200.0) as u32;\n        let pe_bar = ((pe.abs() / scale).min(1.0) * 200.0) as u32;\n\n        let drift = if self.initial_total.is_nan() || self.initial_total.abs() < 1e-9 {\n            0.0_f64\n        } else {\n            (total - self.initial_total) / self.initial_total.abs() * 100.0\n        };\n        let drift_color = if drift.abs() < 1.0 {\n            \"#4ade80\"\n        } else if drift.abs() < 5.0 {\n            \"#facc15\"\n        } else {\n            \"#f87171\"\n        };\n\n        LiveContent::Html(format!(\n            r#\"<div style=\"font-family:monospace;background:#0d1117;color:#e6edf3;padding:16px 20px;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid #30363d;min-width:380px\">\n  <div style=\"font-size:14px;font-weight:700;color:#58a6ff;margin-bottom:12px\">&#x26a1; Energy Dashboard</div>\n  <div style=\"margin-bottom:8px\">\n    <div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;margin-bottom:3px\">\n      <span style=\"color:#f87171\">KE (kinetic)</span>\n      <span style=\"color:#f87171\">{ke:.4} J</span>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"background:#21262d;border-radius:4px;height:10px;width:200px\">\n      <div style=\"background:#f87171;height:10px;border-radius:4px;width:{ke_bar}px\"></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"margin-bottom:8px\">\n    <div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;margin-bottom:3px\">\n      <span style=\"color:#60a5fa\">PE (potential)</span>\n      <span style=\"color:#60a5fa\">{pe:.4} J</span>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"background:#21262d;border-radius:4px;height:10px;width:200px\">\n      <div style=\"background:#60a5fa;height:10px;border-radius:4px;width:{pe_bar}px\"></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"border-top:1px solid #30363d;margin:10px 0;padding-top:10px\">\n    <div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between\">\n      <span>Total energy</span>\n      <span style=\"font-weight:700\">{total:.4} J</span>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;margin-top:4px\">\n      <span>Energy drift</span>\n      <span style=\"color:{drift_color}\">{drift:+.3}%</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"border-top:1px solid #30363d;margin:10px 0;padding-top:10px;font-size:13px\">\n    <div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between\">\n      <span>&#x3c9;&#x2081;</span><span>{omega1:.3} rad/s</span>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;margin-top:4px\">\n      <span>&#x3c9;&#x2082;</span><span>{omega2:.3} rad/s</span>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;margin-top:4px;color:#8b949e\">\n      <span>tick</span><span>{tick}</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\"#,\n            tick = self.tick,\n        ))\n    }\n\n    fn fps() -> u32 {\n        10\n    }\n}",
      "cargo_toml": null,
      "collapsed": true
    }
  ],
  "description": "Model chaotic motion with a live double pendulum simulation: interactive parameter sliders, RK4 physics, and a real-time energy dashboard.",
  "tags": [
    "physics",
    "simulation",
    "chaos",
    "live-simulation",
    "live-view"
  ]
}
